{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A layered drawing by the Sugiyama framework: every vertex on a horizontal layer, edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pointing down, long edges bent through every layer they cross, few crossings.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sugiyamaLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 100) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LayeredDrawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing07LayeredB0V","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/LayeredDrawing","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cycles are broken by reversing the edges of ","type":"text"},{"code":"feedbackArcSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (Eades, Lin and Smyth)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other than self-loops; a DAG reverses nothing. Self-loops are left out of the drawing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Layers minimize the total edge span Σ (layer(target) − layer(source)) with every edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spanning at least one layer, parallel edges counted each (Gansner et al.‘s network","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"simplex, solved through its dual min-cost flow as OGDF’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"OptimalRanking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); each weakly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connected component starts at layer 0. Where several layerings are optimal, which one is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"chosen is not specified.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge spanning k > 1 layers gets a bend point on each of the k − 1 between."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Crossings are reduced by barycenter sweeps: each layer starts with its vertices in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, then its bend points by edge position; a sweep sorts layers 1 … L−1 by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the mean position of each node’s neighbours in the layer above, then layers L−2 … 0 by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"those below, stably, a node with no such neighbour keeping its position. The order with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the fewest crossings seen is kept. Sweeps stop at no crossings, when a sweep changes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing, or after "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (igraph’s default, 100)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"x coordinates are Brandes and Köpf’s: four vertical alignments to median neighbours,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"avoiding type-1 conflicts, each compacted by longest path over its blocks at separation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1, aligned to the narrowest, and averaged by the mean of the two median candidates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Then the least x is 0, and y is the layer.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Layered drawing as a framework: Sugiyama, Tagawa and Toda, “Methods for visual","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"understanding of hierarchical system structures”, IEEE Transactions on Systems, Man, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Cybernetics 11(2), 1981. Layering: Gansner, Koutsofios, North and Vo, “A technique for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drawing directed graphs”, IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering 19(3), 1993.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Coordinates: Brandes and Köpf, “Fast and simple horizontal coordinate assignment”, Graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Drawing (GD 2001), LNCS 2265, 2002. The compaction is longest path rather than the paper’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"class shifts, which Brandes, Walter and Zink show can violate the separation (“Erratum:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Fast and simple horizontal coordinate assignment”, arXiv:2008.01252, 2020).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O((n + m) log n) for cycle removal. Network simplex has no polynomial bound and is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"superlinear in practice: on random DAGs with m = 2n it takes about 60 ms at n = 10⁴ and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0.65 s at 4 · 10⁴, growing about as n^1.5 to n^1.7 (release build). O(maxIterations ·"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(N + M) log N) for crossing reduction over N vertices and bend points and M segments;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(N + M) for coordinates."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations ≥ 0"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/sugiyamaLayout(maxIterations:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"GraphDrawing","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"sugiyamaLayout"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LayeredDrawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing07LayeredB0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P0A7DrawingE14sugiyamaLayout13maxIterationsAD07LayeredD0VyxGSi_tF","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/SugiyamaLayout.swift#L44","fileName":"SugiyamaLayout.swift"},"title":"sugiyamaLayout(maxIterations:)","role":"symbol"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/sugiyamalayout(maxiterations:)"]}],"references":{"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DirectedGraph"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/sugiyamaLayout(maxIterations:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/sugiyamalayout(maxiterations:)","title":"sugiyamaLayout(maxIterations:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/sugiyamaLayout(maxIterations:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sugiyamaLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing07LayeredB0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"LayeredDrawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A layered drawing by the Sugiyama framework: every vertex on a horizontal layer, edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pointing down, long edges bent through every layer they cross, few crossings.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","title":"GraphProtocols","role":"collection"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/LayeredDrawing":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/LayeredDrawing","abstract":[{"text":"A layered drawing of a directed graph (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph.sugiyamaLayout(…)"},{"text":"): a position per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex with y its layer, a layer per vertex, and bend points for every edge that crosses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"layers. Vertices and bend points in one layer are at least 1 apart; edges point down once the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reversed ones are turned.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/layereddrawing","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LayeredDrawing","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LayeredDrawing","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"LayeredDrawing"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","kind":"symbol","title":"GraphDrawing","role":"collection"}}}